{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Do not fear him.</b> For Moses was afraid to wage war against him — lest the merit of Abraham stand for him, as it is written ״וַיָּבֹא הַפָּלִיט״ (Genesis 14) — that is Og, who escaped from the Refa'im whom Kedarla'omer and his allies had smitten at Ashterot Karnayim, as it is written (Deuteronomy 3) ״רַק עוֹג מֶלֶךְ הַבָּשָׁן נִשְׁאַר מִיֶּתֶר הָרְפָאִים״ (Niddah 61)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:06.981290362Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}